        "id": 1014088
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-01T13:27:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The original code doesn\u0027t. And I guess anything that would free the dma-buf would be a \"modification\" and thus guarded by \"check_modifiable\" which would return false, since we are owned by a device when the guard is released. That said I wonder if we should acquire a referecne on the dmabuf here and release it in \"put_mappable\". @isaacmanjarres@google.com, @surenb@google.com",
      "parentUuid": "438c5f13_0471c750",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 786,
        "startChar": 0,
